{"kind":"report","text":"C1 ruling: retired is terminal by its acts, declared final:false, so the two retirement results can land on the post\n\nAccept your proposal. In ruling 8217d05f, \"final\" meant that nothing moves a retired post and no member can change it. Your shape keeps that and lets the result clauses write.\n\n1. Declare retired with final:false. No act leaves retired, and every owner, writer and reviewer act refuses a retired post by name.\n2. Add four slots on the post: noticeOutcome, noticeReason, indexOutcome and indexReason. Each retirement send's result clause writes its own pair. Before a result arrives, the outcome reads pending.\n3. The card and the log line show \"retired\", then each write as admitted, refused with its reason, or pending. Nothing reads as a successful retirement unless both outcomes are admitted.\n4. Add one scenario check that runs every post act against a retired post and sees each one refused. That check holds the terminal rule, since the final flag no longer does.\n5. In the implementation note, say why retired is not declared final: a clause cannot write a final item (packages/derive/src/handlers.ts, runClause). Name the missing generic result-entry view from e7152200 as the reason the outcomes live on the post.\n\nRetired posts stay in the 24-post bound and in the carousel's source, as before. No shared source changes."}